{"id": "P-1", "klass": "meta vs meta.schema.json drift", "title": "component meta-schema sweep", "script": "probe_meta_schema.py", "environment": "sandbox", "blind": "grammar only — a meta can name the wrong token, the wrong component or a nonexistent edge target and still pass; it cannot see a schema that is itself wrong (widen-vs-repair is an OPEN QUESTION TO DAVE from #204, untouched here); EXAMPLE-button.meta.json is a DECLARED exemption printed on every run.", "caught": [{"session": 204, "date": "2026-08-19", "defect": "three authored metas failed Draft7 validation (document-row stateModel enum + unexpected edge types + non-$ annotation keys; payment-card-visual and runway-bar wrote 300-char prose into the provenance.source ENUM) — 92 metas, PASS=88 FAIL=4, with the whole gate chain green", "receipt": "notes/_receipts/2026-08-19-204-verifier-challenge-table.md:30", "provenance": "historical-mined", "kind": "exact", "note": "verifier challenge C-8. Repaired the same session — notes/_receipts/2026-08-19-204-buildpm-claim-table.md:257 (FIX 1), AFTER PASS=91 FAIL=1."}], "note": "ONE distinct session in the ledger — deliberately NOT twice-caught. The #204 catch and the #204 repair are the same occasion and _promote.py counts occasions, not entries."}
{"id": "P-2", "klass": "duplicate id + unresolved IDREF in review pages", "title": "duplicate-ID/IDREF scan", "script": "probe_dup_ids.py", "environment": "sandbox", "blind": "ids or references built by JavaScript · whether a RESOLVED reference points at the right element (presence only) · anything outside the glob (reviews/REVIEW-*.html) · fragment href misses are WARN tier by inherited #204 judgment, never findings.", "caught": [{"session": 204, "date": "2026-08-19", "defect": "three of six review pages shipped every id 8× (one per theme pane); seven of eight progressbars took their accessible name from the mono/light pane via aria-labelledby, and pcv-contactless ×8 was the same shape for an SVG reference", "receipt": "notes/_receipts/2026-08-19-204-verifier-challenge-table.md:109", "provenance": "historical-mined", "kind": "exact", "note": "verifier NEW-1; repaired at notes/_receipts/2026-08-19-204-buildpm-claim-table.md:265 (FIX 2) — six pages to DUP=0, unresolved_aria=0."}, {"session": 206, "date": "2026-08-19", "defect": "FIRST DRIVE OF THIS PROBE: 46 findings across 45 review pages — REVIEW-203-kpi-tile (kpi-down/kpi-table/kpi-up ×8 each), REVIEW-203-timeline (tl1-h/tl2-h/tl3-h ×8 each) and REVIEW-203-time-picker (aria-describedby='f-time-help' unresolved ×8). The #204 class survives on the #203-era pages, which the #204 repair never touched.", "receipt": "notes/_receipts/2026-08-19-206-w45-registry-drive.md", "provenance": "live-run", "kind": "exact"}], "note": "TWICE-CAUGHT, MIXED basis: one mined receipt (#204) + one live catch (#206)."}
{"id": "P-3", "klass": "dangling var renders silent black (dataviz)", "title": "dangling-var PIXEL test (render + cascade + pixel)", "script": "probe_dangling_var_pixel.py", "environment": "sandbox-render", "blind": "a var that resolves to the WRONG colour · zero-area elements (reported PIXEL-UNSAMPLED, never clean) · script-set colours after the settle window · themes other than the page default · small antialiased glyphs may carry NO exact rgb(0,0,0) pixel, so the pixel leg is corroboration and the cascade leg is the detector · UNPROVEN IN CI (#173 split; s204-D1 item 5 owns the CI leg).", "caught": [{"session": 184, "date": "2026-08-16", "defect": "MEASURED by mutation drive: a rect with fill=var(--status-breach) and the property declared nowhere paints pure black and was reported a PASS by thirteen of thirteen gates", "receipt": "knowledge/_DS-IMPROVEMENTS.md:1973", "provenance": "historical-mined", "kind": "exact", "note": "s184-D3 drive; the static markup gate _gate_dataviz_vars.py was built for this class at #190 and declares per-SELECTOR scope as a blind spot — this probe is the render that covers it."}, {"session": 204, "date": "2026-08-19", "defect": "a self-referential mapping --border-radius-surface: var(--border-radius-surface) resolved to the CSS initial value and killed Console's 20px surface radius across 8 panes — no error, no gate, and the wrong value (0px) is the house default so it reads as correct", "receipt": "notes/_receipts/2026-08-19-204-wave-laneP-fintech-visuals.md:174", "provenance": "historical-mined", "kind": "species", "note": "SPECIES, not the same scan: a CYCLE, not an absent declaration. Counted only under --include-species, and the #204 verifier CONTRADICTED it as a shipped defect (zero occurrences on disk) — recorded so the widened count is never read as the strict one."}], "note": "EXACT count = 1 session, so NOT a candidate under the strict rule today. That is the honest reading: the class was proven once, by mutation, and has not recurred in a scan since."}
