{"id": "P-6", "klass": "browser begins ENACTING text-box-trim inside form controls (library-wide field shift, no commit)", "title": "input leading-trim enactment CANARY", "script": "probe_input_trim_enactment.py", "environment": "sandbox-render", "blind": "WHICH components move and by how much (it measures the MECHANISM on a self-contained fixture, never the 65 snippets) · engines other than the one this environment can launch — a Gecko or WebKit enactment lands unseen until this probe runs there · partial enactment across the seven typed inputs (the fixture carries type=text, the representative case) · whether the enacted result is DESIRABLE, which is Dave's eye and is exactly what the finding asks for · the repo's own authored CSS — removing the input vocabulary from the snippets does NOT silence this probe, because the fixture carries its own declaration.", "caught": [], "note": "⛔ A CANARY, AND ITS GREEN IS AN INVERSION: findings=0 means the engine STILL does not enact text-box-trim inside a form control — the inert state Dave reviewed at #209 (W-61) and ruled KEEP on. findings=1 is the day a browser changes, with nothing in this repo changing at all, which is why no static gate can cover the class. The ledger is DELIBERATELY EMPTY: the class has never been caught, because it has not happened yet — the #209 measurement (span 32.00→11.56px / button 32.00→11.02px vs input 32.00→32.00px, 0 input boxes changed height across the whole sweep) is the BASELINE, not a catch, and recording it as one would be a mined receipt read as a live catch. _promote.py therefore counts 0 sessions for P-6, correctly. Baseline receipt: reviews/REVIEW-209-input-trim-before-after-v1.html. Threshold declared in the script: shrink >= 1.00 CSS px AND >= 5%. The positive-control <span> failing to move is a REFUSAL (77), not a pass — an engine that trims nothing was never asked the question."}
{"id": "P-7", "klass": "@container rule aimed at its own container (the rule can never fire)", "title": "container self-query scan", "script": "probe_container_self_query.py", "environment": "sandbox", "blind": "EXACT whitespace-normalised selector-string overlap ONLY — `@container{ .a .b{} }` against `.b{container-type}` is the same defect and is MISSED (the conservative matching is the price of zero false positives, declared not designed away) · the DOM: it never asks whether an element matching the selector exists, nor whether one nests INSIDE another matching the same selector, so a finding means 'dead for the outermost match', not 'dead for all' (Layout-utilities' own demo nests a .l-split inside a .l-split, and the inner one fires legally) · a container established in another file or by JavaScript · container-name split across rules · WARN tier by design: an overlap in a file that declares OTHER containers is REPORTED and NOT counted, because one of those may legally host the query (the .tpl-split-host repair shape) · anything outside knowledge/snippets/*.reference.html.", "caught": [{"session": 210, "date": "2026-08-20", "defect": "Template-auth's first draft declared container-type:inline-size on `.auth` and then wrote `@container (max-width:880px){ .auth{ grid-template-columns:1fr } }` — THE TWO PANELS NEVER COLLAPSED, and the 420px screenshot 'looked plausible enough to accept'. Repaired by moving the container onto `.auth-shell`.", "receipt": "notes/_receipts/2026-08-20-210-wave5-laneC-form-templates.md:20", "provenance": "historical-mined", "kind": "exact", "note": "The same receipt at :286 PRICED this probe and did not build it — 'A GATE CANDIDATE, PRICED, NOT BUILT … the conductor's, and Dave's to promote.' This script is that candidate, built."}, {"session": 210, "date": "2026-08-20", "defect": "Hero-variants declared container-type:inline-size on `.hv-media` and the @container rule targeting `.hv-media`'s own grid-template-columns queried `.hv-media`'s nearest ANCESTOR container, which did not exist — the media split silently never collapsed, while a sibling rule against the container it DID establish fired, producing a visually plausible half-repair. Fixed with a new `.hv-frame` wrapper.", "receipt": "notes/_receipts/2026-08-20-210-wave6-laneC-lockups.md:152", "provenance": "historical-mined", "kind": "exact"}, {"session": 210, "date": "2026-08-20", "defect": "COMPOSITION RULE 12: the GATED PRIMITIVE Layout-utilities carries the defect on `.l-split` itself. Measured at #210 — Layout-utilities @1400px computes `grid-template-columns: 90px 280px` under a caption claiming it 'has already collapsed'; @420px the top-level split computes `44px 280px`; the dashboard before its workaround measured a 26px chart stage on a phone with every gate green. The lane could not edit the gated parent and added a `.tpl-split-host` wrapper instead.", "receipt": "knowledge/snippets/Template-dashboard.reference.html:264", "provenance": "historical-mined", "kind": "exact", "note": "⬛ THE REAL REPAIR IS DAVE'S, in the primitive's own words: give `.l-split` a HOST, or move container-type onto a wrapper inside Layout-utilities. Still OPEN on disk."}, {"session": 210, "date": "2026-08-20", "defect": "FIRST DRIVE OF THIS PROBE: 6 findings + 3 WARN across 135 snippets. The 6 are the UNREPAIRED `.l-split` primitive travelling — Layout-utilities:242 and the copies in Template-confirmation/-empty/-error/-report — plus a SEVENTH INSTANCE NOBODY HAD NAMED: Transfer-list.reference.html:90, `.tl{container-type:inline-size}` at :53 targeted by `@container (max-width:480px){ .tl{flex-direction:column} }`, the file's only container. The 3 WARN are Template-dashboard/-detail/-settings, where the `.tpl-split-host` workaround supplies a legal host.", "receipt": "knowledge/snippets/Layout-utilities.reference.html:242", "provenance": "live-run", "kind": "exact", "note": "⚠ NO LANE RECEIPT EXISTS for this drive — the build lane wrote none, so the pointer is at the DEFECT ITSELF (probeable, `s182-D1`) rather than at a document about it. Homing a receipt is the conductor's."}], "note": "⛔ FOUR ledger entries, ONE distinct session (210) — `_promote.py` counts OCCASIONS, not entries, so this probe counts as caught ONCE and is NOT a twice-caught candidate today. That is the honest reading and it is written here so the four rows are never miscounted as four occasions (the P-1 shape). The three mined entries and the live drive are all 2026-08-20. ⬛ ADVISORY: promotion to a blocking gate is DAVE'S (derivation governance); this row does not propose it. ⚠ THE PROBE IS NOT GREEN ON THE CURRENT TREE and that is the point — 6 findings stand, all rooted in one unrepaired primitive whose repair Layout-utilities' own consumers already recorded as Dave's."}
{"id": "P-8", "klass": "dangling var(--x) — the property is declared nowhere reachable in the file (TEXT tier)", "title": "dangling-var TEXT scan (no browser)", "script": "probe_dangling_var_text.py", "environment": "sandbox", "blind": "THE CASCADE — it asks 'is this name declared ANYWHERE in the file', not 'is it declared on an ancestor of the element that reads it'; a --x declared on `.a` and read on an unrelated `.b` dangles AT RUNTIME and this probe calls it clean (that is P-3's job from pixels, and _gate_dataviz_vars.py's per-selector job) · a var that resolves to the WRONG value · a var declared but never read (dead, not dangling) · properties injected by a stylesheet the file does not <link>, or by script from another file · references built by string concatenation in JS · references outside <style> blocks and inline style attributes · var(--x, fallback) is EXEMPT by design — a fallback is the author saying out loud the property may be absent · anything outside knowledge/snippets/*.reference.html.", "caught": [{"session": 184, "date": "2026-08-16", "defect": "MEASURED by mutation drive: a rect with fill=var(--status-breach) and the property declared nowhere paints pure black and was reported a PASS by thirteen of thirteen gates", "receipt": "knowledge/_DS-IMPROVEMENTS.md:1973", "provenance": "historical-mined", "kind": "exact", "note": "⚠ THE SAME OCCASION IS ALSO IN P-3's LEDGER, deliberately and declared: P-3 asks this class FROM PIXELS and needs a browser, P-8 asks it FROM TEXT in the sandbox (#173 environment split). One defect, two instruments, two rows — a reader counting occasions across probes must not double-count session 184."}, {"session": 210, "date": "2026-08-20", "defect": "`--muted` DANGLED IN TWO FILES AND NOTHING VISIBLE COULD EVER HAVE SHOWN IT — Template-error and Template-confirmation borrowed Confirmation's `color:var(--muted)` and never declared `--muted`, so the colour fell to inherit; --muted is text/secondary, which in Mono is the SAME HEX as text/default, so no pixel, no gate and no eye could see it. Repaired by declaring it in both theme blocks of both files.", "receipt": "notes/_receipts/2026-08-20-210-wave6-laneB-p3-templates.md:151", "provenance": "historical-mined", "kind": "exact"}, {"session": 210, "date": "2026-08-20", "defect": "FIRST DRIVE OF THIS PROBE: 58 findings in 9 of 135 snippets, in TWO shapes. (a) COMMENTED-OUT ×46 — in FIVE files (Button, Chart-butterfly-h, Template-dashboard, Template-detail, Template-list-index) the generated AUTO-TOKENS :root block was injected INSIDE an unclosed HTML comment: Button.reference.html line 45 opens `<!-- TYPE-001 · canon type composites. MUST come BEFORE the component <style>` and the generator appended the token block after that literal `<style>` TEXT, so the whole alpha ramp is comment, not CSS, and every var(--alpha-NN) in those files dangles. (b) ABSENT ×12 — --header/--fborder/--error/--error-tint/--success/--success-tint/--warning/--warning-tint read by demo-chrome and status rules in Template-confirmation/-empty/-error/-settings and declared nowhere: the #210 --muted shape, unrepaired, in four more files.", "receipt": "knowledge/snippets/Button.reference.html:45", "provenance": "live-run", "kind": "exact", "note": "⚠ NO LANE RECEIPT EXISTS for this drive — the build lane wrote none, so the pointer is at the DEFECT ITSELF (probeable, `s182-D1`). ⛔ NOTHING WAS FIXED: this probe reports, and the repair (and whether shape (a) is a GENERATOR defect in gen_token_ramp.py rather than a per-file one) is the conductor's and Dave's."}], "note": "TWO distinct sessions (184, 210), MIXED basis — but see the session-184 entry's note: that occasion is SHARED with P-3 by design and must not be double-counted when reading the two ledgers together. ⬛ ADVISORY, registered like P-5/P-6: promotion to a blocking gate is DAVE'S (derivation governance). ★ The external vocabulary is PARSED from whatever stylesheets each file actually <link>s (measured today: ../canon/type.css → --uf/--cap/--desc/--slot) and is never hand-typed — a typed allowlist is a carried figure and rots. ⚠ THE PROBE IS NOT GREEN ON THE CURRENT TREE: 58 findings stand, reported and NOT repaired."}
